Package: devnet
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sajjad Mohabati <sajjadmohabati@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3:any (>= 3.9), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, librsvg2-common, iproute2, iputils-ping, pkexec | policykit-1, libglib2.0-bin, desktop-file-utils, gtk-update-icon-cache, hicolor-icon-theme
Recommends: fonts-inter, network-manager, systemd-resolved, iso-codes, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/SajjadMohabati/DevNet
Description: Split tunneling, DNS switching and local dev servers
 DevNet keeps selected networks, hosts, domains and country IP ranges on
 your LAN gateway, outside every VPN. It repairs the routes when Wi-Fi or a
 VPN changes, switches DNS on every active link (including VPN links), runs a
 Cloudflare speed test, and lists local development servers and containers.
 .
 The app lives in the system tray, includes a compact panel and a native GTK4
 window, and uses a small polkit-scoped helper for privileged operations.
